Some more door ideas:
---------------------

I don't like the idea someone had about getting damage when bumping into a
closed door (you don't get damaged when bumping into a wall!).  I think
damage would be unacceptable under normal conditions, but resonable when
blinded, and possible confused or halucinating.  Monsters should be able to
knock down doors.  (I haven't seen this happen.  Can they?)  It would be
nice to see something like:

"The blade of a black knife thrusts through the door.  The door weakens."
or "The door crashes down" (Then, say, an umber hulk enters).  The door
could "crash down on you" if you happen to be standing next to it.  

Perhaps if you were standing against the door, weapons could come through the
doors could "get you."

The doors could also have non-regenerable "hit points."  When a door reachs
zero it breaks down (and essentially disappears).  Differt door types could
exist like weak balsa, strong oak, metal, or see-through glass.  How about:

"The killer bee bounces off the glass door while attempting to sting you."

Some monsters might always break down doors, and others only when Aggrevate
Monsters was one of your attributes (if you don't know what the means,
don't worry - I'm not talking about the ring).

Fire breathing dragons could set wooden doors on fire.  Metal doors might
just glow red. (Or white, or orange, depending on the creature's distance
from the door).

Also, a character with a screwdriver could take a door off its hinges
and (if strong enough carry it away).  Later he could put the door
up someplace else if the frame had hinges and he haden't lost the pins.

Gosh!  There's so many possibilities...
